.\" Man page for flow-pipeline(5)
.\" Generated from SUMMARY_OF_AVAILABLE_OPTIONS.md
.TH FLOW-PIPELINE 5 "November 2026" "ETL Madness Flow" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
flow-pipeline \- XML pipeline specification and element reference for flow(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I scripts.xml
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Flow pipeline document is an XML file rooted at a
.B <pipeline>
element that declares database connections, initial variables, optional preflight checks, and sequential, conditional, looping, transactional, or parallel workflow tasks executed by
.BR flow (1).
.PP
Attribute names on XML elements are case-insensitive and support
.IR snake_case ,
.I kebab-case
.RB ( \- ),
and dot
.RB ( . )
separators.
Supported attributes and body text allow variable interpolation using
.B {{VariableName}}
placeholders.
.SH TOP-LEVEL STRUCTURE
A
.B <pipeline>
document may contain the following top-level child sections:
.IP 1. 4
.B <databases>
\(em optional collection of named relational SQL and Key-Value database connections.
.IP 2. 4
.B <variables>
\(em optional collection of typed initial pipeline variables.
.IP 3. 4
.B <preflight>
\(em optional container of setup, smoke-test, or connectivity validation nodes executed before
.B <flow>
(or standalone when
.B flow \-preflight
is passed).
.IP 4. 4
.B <flow>
\(em main execution container whose child nodes execute in document order unless altered by control-flow elements.
.SH DATABASES (<databases> AND <database>)
The optional
.B <databases>
container accepts an optional
.I description
attribute and zero or more
.B <database>
elements.
Each
.B <database>
defines a named connection handle and pool configuration:
.TP
.B name
(Mandatory) Unique handle referenced by
.IR db ,
.IR database ,
or
.I target_db
on pipeline task nodes.
.TP
.B id
Optional identifier for the database definition.
.TP
.BR driver ", " type
Database driver name.
Relational SQL drivers:
.B sqlserver
(default when omitted),
.BR postgres ,
.BR mysql ,
.BR sqlite ,
.BR oracle .
Key-Value drivers:
.B bbolt
.RB ( bolt ),
.BR badger ,
.B redis
.RB ( valkey ),
.BR etcd .
.TP
.B connection_string
(Mandatory) Driver-specific DSN, URL, or file/directory path.
Supports
.B {{VariableName}}
interpolation.
.TP
.B workload
Optional pool tuning profile:
.B oltp
(default),
.BR bulk ,
.BR analytics ,
or
.BR batch .
Selects workload-tuned pool defaults when individual pool attributes are omitted:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
.BR oltp " (or omitted): "
.IR max_open_conns =25,
.IR max_idle_conns =10,
.IR conn_max_lifetime =5m,
.IR conn_max_idle_time =2m.
.IP \(bu 3
.BR bulk ": "
.IR max_open_conns =50,
.IR max_idle_conns =25,
.IR conn_max_lifetime =30m,
.IR conn_max_idle_time =10m.
.IP \(bu 3
.BR analytics ": "
.IR max_open_conns =15,
.IR max_idle_conns =8,
.IR conn_max_lifetime =30m,
.IR conn_max_idle_time =10m.
.IP \(bu 3
.BR batch ": "
.IR max_open_conns =20,
.IR max_idle_conns =10,
.IR conn_max_lifetime =15m,
.IR conn_max_idle_time =5m.
.RE
.TP
.B max_open_conns
Maximum simultaneous open connections in the pool.
.TP
.B max_idle_conns
Maximum idle connections retained in the pool (clamped to
.IR max_open_conns ).
.TP
.BR conn_max_lifetime_seconds ", " conn_max_lifetime
Maximum duration a connection may be reused before recycling (accepts Go durations like
.B 5m
or integer seconds).
.TP
.BR conn_max_idle_time_seconds ", " conn_max_idle_time
Maximum duration an idle connection remains in the pool before closing (accepts Go durations like
.B 2m
or integer seconds).
.TP
.B description
Human-readable description of the database connection.
.SH VARIABLES (<variables> AND <variable>)
The optional
.B <variables>
container holds zero or more
.B <variable>
elements:
.TP
.B name
(Mandatory) Variable name used for retrieval and
.B {{VariableName}}
interpolation.
.TP
.B value
(Mandatory) Initial variable value parsed according to
.IR type .
.TP
.B type
Data type:
.B string
(default),
.BR int " / " integer ,
.BR bool " / " boolean ,
.BR float " / " double " / " float64 ,
.BR datetime ,
or
.BR date .
.TP
.BR id ", " description
Optional identifier and human-readable description.
.SH CONTROL FLOW AND LOGICAL GROUPING
The following control-flow elements are permitted inside
.B <preflight>
and
.BR <flow> :
.SS <foreach>
Executes nested child steps once per row returned by a SQL driver query.
Sets
.B LOOP_INDEX
to the zero-based row index on each iteration and exposes returned columns as pipeline variables in original, lowercase, and uppercase forms.
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.B db
/
.B database
(mandatory),
.IR id ,
.B language
/
.B lang
(default
.BR sql ),
.B var
/
.B variable
(takes precedence over inline SQL text when non-empty), inline SQL query before child elements.
.SS <group>
Organizes nested steps into a sequential block with optional conditional execution, database transaction wrapping, or dedicated connection pinning.
.IP \(bu 3
Identity & timeout:
.IR id " / " name ,
.IR timeout
(e.g.,
.BR 30s ,
.BR 5m ),
.IR description .
.IP \(bu 3
Condition attributes:
.IR var " / " if_var ,
.IR equals " / " val " / " value " / " if_val " / " if_equals ,
.IR condition " / " cond .
.IP \(bu 3
Database transaction & session attributes:
.B transaction
/
.B tx
(boolean, default
.BR false ;
rolls back on child failure, commits on completion),
.B session
/
.B pin_connection
/
.B pin_conn
/
.B sticky
(boolean, default
.BR false ;
pins a single
.I *sql.Conn
so session-scoped temporary tables like
.B #Temp
or
.B CREATE TEMP TABLE
persist across child steps and nested transactional groups),
.B db
/
.B database
(mandatory when
.I transaction
or
.I session
is
.BR true ).
.SS <while>
Repeatedly executes nested steps while a condition evaluates to true, setting
.B WHILE_INDEX
to the zero-based iteration index.
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.IR id ,
.IR var " / " if_var ,
.IR equals " / " val " / " value " / " if_val " / " if_equals ,
.IR condition " / " cond ,
.B max_iterations
/
.B max_loops
(default
.B 1000
to prevent unbounded loops).
.SS <if>, <then>, <else>
Conditionally executes
.B <then>
(or direct inline child nodes) when the condition passes, or
.B <else>
when the condition fails.
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes on
.BR <if> :
.IR id ,
.IR var " / " if_var ,
.IR equals " / " val " / " value " / " if_val " / " if_equals ,
.IR condition " / " cond ,
.IR description .
.SS <parallel>
Executes nested child steps concurrently across a worker goroutine pool.
Branch variable states are isolated during execution and merged upon completion with automatic collision namespacing
.RB ( WORKER_<id>_<key> ).
Context cancellation propagates across branches on error.
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.B max_threads
/
.B threads
/
.B concurrency
(default
.B 0
/ unbounded: runs all child branches concurrently).
.SH PIPELINE TASK ELEMENTS
All task elements below may appear under
.BR <flow> ,
.BR <preflight> ,
or nested inside control-flow blocks.
Most data-producing steps store their output in
.B LAST_OUTPUT
in addition to any configured output variable.
.SS <template> and <template_html>
Render Go templates using current pipeline variables.
.B <template>
uses
.I text/template
 while
.B <template_html>
uses
.I html/template
with automatic HTML escaping against XSS.
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.B id
(mandatory),
.IR name ,
.I file
(mutually exclusive with inline template body),
.IR engine ,
.IR output_var " / " var ,
.I mode
.RB ( summary
returns brief status; unset returns rendered text).
.SS <sql>
Executes a SQL statement against a configured database connection.
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.B db
/
.B database
(mandatory),
.IR id ,
.IR var " / " variable
(SQL source variable; overrides inline body when non-empty),
.IR output_var " / " out_var " / " output_variable ,
and inline SQL statement body.
.SS <sql_bulk>
Streams rows returned by a source SQL query into a destination table.
Uses native TDS
.B CopyIn
for SQL Server and prepared multi-row batched
.B INSERT
statements for PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle, and SQLite (automatically capping batch size to dialect parameter limits: 65,535 for PostgreSQL/MySQL, 32,767 for Oracle, 32,766 for SQLite).
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.B db
/
.B database
(mandatory source connection),
.B target_table
(mandatory destination table; supports
.B {{var}}
placeholders),
.IR target_db " / " target_database
(defaults to source
.IR db ),
.IR batch_size ,
.IR var " / " variable ,
.IR output_var " / " out_var
(receives copied row count),
SQL Server bulk options
.B tablock
(default
.BR true ),
.B check_constraints
(default
.BR false ),
.B fire_triggers
(default
.BR false ),
.B keep_nulls
(default
.BR false ),
and inline source SQL query.
.SS <kv>
Executes atomic Key-Value operations against
.BR bbolt ,
.BR badger ,
.BR redis ,
or
.BR etcd .
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.B db
/
.B database
(mandatory),
.IR id ,
.B bucket
(bucket or key prefix; default
.BR default ),
.B op
.RB ( get ,
.BR put " / " set ,
.BR delete " / " del ,
.BR scan " / " list ),
.IR key ,
.IR value ,
.IR var " / " variable ,
.IR output_var " / " out_var " / " output_variable ,
or inline DSL command text (for example,
.B "set user:101 Alice"
or
.BR "get user:101" ).
.SS <kv_bulk>
Streams rows from a relational SQL query (projected column 1 = key, column 2 = value) into a Key-Value store in batches.
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.B db
/
.B database
(mandatory SQL source),
.B target_db
/
.B target_database
(mandatory KV target),
.B target_bucket
/
.B bucket
(mandatory),
.B batch_size
(default
.BR 10000 ),
.IR var " / " variable ,
.IR output_var " / " out_var ,
and inline SQL query.
.SS <assert>
Evaluates a pipeline variable against an expected value and triggers failure handling when unmet.
.IP \(bu 3
Attributes:
.B var
(mandatory),
.IR equals " / " value ,
.IR operator ,
.IR message ,
.B on_failure
.RB ( halt
[default],
.BR warn ,
or
.BR continue ),
.IR fail_var ,
.B fail_val
(default
.BR true ),
.IR id ,
.IR description ,
and optional nested
.B <on_failure>
child nodes executed prior to halting or continuing.
.SS <file_read> and <file_save>
Read local file contents into a variable or write variable/inline text to a local file (creating parent directories automatically).
.IP \(bu 3
.BR <file_read> :
path via
.IR file " / " path " / " filename ;
output variable via
.IR var " / " variable " / " output_var " / " output_variable " / " out_var ;
optional
.IR id .
.IP \(bu 3
.BR <file_save> :
destination via
.IR file " / " path " / " filename ;
payload via
.IR var " / " variable
or inline body (with
.B {{var}}
interpolation);
.B append
(boolean, default
.B false
overwrites); optional
.IR id .
.SS <excel_write> and <excel_read>
Create/update or read
.I .xlsx
Excel workbooks.
.IP \(bu 3
.BR <excel_write> :
.B file
(mandatory
.I .xlsx
path),
.B sheet
(default
.BR Sheet1 ),
.B db
and inline SQL query (writes column headers to row 1 and query rows beneath), optional
.IR id .
.IP \(bu 3
.BR <excel_read> :
.B file
(mandatory
.I .xlsx
path),
.I sheet
(defaults to first worksheet),
.B header
(default
.BR true ;
uses first row as JSON object keys),
.IR output_var " / " var
(receives JSON array of row objects), optional
.IR id .
.SS <json_path>, <yaml_path>, and <xml_xpath>
Extract values or nodes from structured documents in files or variables.
.IP \(bu 3
.BR <json_path> :
source via
.I file
or
.IR var ;
query via
.IR path " / " jsonpath
or inline body;
.B mode
.RB ( value
[default],
.BR json ,
.BR json_array );
destination via
.IR output_var " / " out_var .
.IP \(bu 3
.BR <yaml_path> :
source via
.I file
or
.IR var ;
query via
.IR path " / " yamlpath
or inline body;
.B mode
.RB ( value
[default],
.BR json ,
.BR json_array ,
.BR yaml );
destination via
.IR output_var " / " out_var .
.IP \(bu 3
.BR <xml_xpath> :
source via
.I file
or
.IR var ;
query via
.I xpath
or inline body;
.B mode
.RB ( text
[default],
.BR xml ,
.BR json_array );
mandatory
.BR output_var .
.SS <http_client>
Sends an HTTP/HTTPS request with variable interpolation and stores the response body and status code.
.IP \(bu 3
Core attributes:
.B uri
/
.B url
(mandatory),
.B method
(default
.BR GET ),
.I data
or inline payload,
.I headers
(comma-, semicolon-, or newline-separated
.I "Name: Value"
pairs),
.IR content_type ,
response body variable
.IR var " / " variable " / " output_var " / " output_variable " / " out_var ,
status code variable
.IR status_code_var " / " status_code_variable " / " status_var " / " status_variable .
.IP \(bu 3
Transport, redirect & TLS attributes:
.IR timeout ,
.IR follow_redirects ,
.IR max_redirects ,
.IR cookie_jar ,
.IR proxy ,
.IR tls_insecure_skip_verify ,
.IR tls_handshake_timeout ,
.IR tls_server_name ,
.IR tls_min_version ,
.IR tls_max_version ,
.IR disable_keep_alives ,
.IR disable_compression ,
.IR max_idle_conns ,
.I max_idle_conns_per_host
(default
.BR 10 ),
.IR max_conns_per_host ,
.IR idle_conn_timeout ,
.IR response_header_timeout ,
.IR expect_continue_timeout ,
.IR max_response_header_bytes ,
.IR write_buffer_size ,
.IR read_buffer_size ,
.IR force_attempt_http2 .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
<pipeline>
  <databases>
    <database name="analytics_db" driver="postgres" workload="analytics"
      connection_string="host=localhost port=5432 user=postgres password={{DB_PASSWORD}} dbname=analytics sslmode=disable" />
  </databases>
  <variables>
    <variable name="BatchDate" type="string" value="2026-10-10" />
  </variables>
  <preflight>
    <sql id="ping" db="analytics_db" output_var="OK">SELECT 'ready'</sql>
    <assert var="OK" equals="ready" on_failure="halt" />
  </preflight>
  <flow>
    <group id="daily_load" db="analytics_db" session="true" transaction="true">
      <sql id="extract" db="analytics_db" output_var="ROW_CNT">
        SELECT COUNT(*) FROM events WHERE event_date = '{{BatchDate}}'
      </sql>
    </group>
  </flow>
</pipeline>
.fi
